  "description": "A fire-rating story is recorded under the literal comparison (\"60 min\" against \"1.5 h\"); Wednesday's \"90 min\" still differs literally and continues it. A Friday normalization of the project names the fixture fire-rating interpretation (version 1). It is an event in the work: the story ends on Friday, cause normalization, with the normalization as its ending record, while Tuesday and Thursday frames still show it open and disagreeing. A Thursday reader naming the interpretation is told the sides match, without changing the standing. The detections keep their recorded literal frame, and the normalization is not among the story's acts.",
  "note": "7.3.8: \"It is an event in the work, not a recorded interpretation: it applies from its effective time, and the record's account before then is never rewritten by it.\" 7.2.6(d): a conflict story ends at \"*normalization*: the interpretation in force for the subject changes while the sides disagree (7.3.8), and under the interpretation in force from then their applicable values are equal, at the instant of that change.\" So the story ends at Friday's normalization, not on Wednesday, and the Thursday frame reads it open.",
